.TH FSTATAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fstatat \- get metadata relative to a directory descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/stat.h>
.PP
.BI "int fstatat(int " directory ", const char* " path ","
.BI "            struct stat* " buffer ", int " flags ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stores metadata in the writable Linux x86\-64
.B struct stat
structure described in
.BR stat (3crunch).
A relative path is resolved from the open directory descriptor, or the current
working directory if it is
.BR AT_FDCWD .
An absolute path ignores the descriptor.
With flags zero, the final symbolic link is followed;
.B AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW
reports the link itself.
.B AT_EMPTY_PATH
allows an empty path to identify the descriptor itself.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged, or \-1 on failure with positive Linux
.BR errno .
.SH NOTES
This wrapper uses Linux x86\-64
.BR newfstatat (2).
Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stat (3crunch),
.BR openat (3crunch),
.BR fstatat (2)
